-- title:
--   q ↦ qᵖ raises the Γ₁(N)∩Γ₀(Nt) level by p
-- statement:
--   Let $N$, $t$ and $p$ be natural numbers with $N$ and $t$ nonzero and $p$ prime, and let $y$ be a Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$. The hypothesis is that $y$ lies in `x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ N (N * t)`, that is, in the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the set `intFormRatiosC ℚ (Gamma1 N ⊓ Gamma0 (N * t))` attached to the congruence subgroup $\Gamma_1(N)\cap\Gamma_0(Nt)$ of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$. The conclusion is that its image under `qExpand ℚ p` lies in `x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ N (N * t * p)`, the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by `intFormRatiosC ℚ (Gamma1 N ⊓ Gamma0 (N * t * p))`. Here `qExpand ℚ p` is the ring homomorphism of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ obtained by embedding the domain of a Hahn series along multiplication by $p$ on $\mathbb{Z}$, i.e. the substitution $q \mapsto q^{p}$ on $q$-expansions, which multiplies every exponent by $p$. Thus substituting $q^p$ for $q$ carries the $q$-expansion function field of level $\Gamma_1(N)\cap\Gamma_0(Nt)$ into that of level $\Gamma_1(N)\cap\Gamma_0(Ntp)$.
--
--   This is the $\Gamma_1\cap\Gamma_0$ form of the classical statement that if $f$ is a modular function for $\Gamma_1(N)\cap\Gamma_0(Nt)$ then $\tau \mapsto f(p\tau)$ is one for $\Gamma_1(N)\cap\Gamma_0(Ntp)$, read on $q$-expansions. It supplies the degeneracy map used in the construction of the Hecke operator at $p$ on the function fields of the modular curves, and is cited in [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_fin_span_heckeRoof_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_fin_span_heckeRoof_x1_mul).
